+<main><h1>Vireek — logo concepts</h1><p class="lead">Three wordmark concepts, original geometric letterforms (no typeface), outlined. Each is shown on light and dark, then at 96/64/32/24/16 px for the symbol and 48/32/24/16 px (height) for the wordmark.</p>
+<div class="grid"><article class="card"><h2>Concept A — Pulse tittle <span class="rec">Recommended · shipped</span></h2><p class="idea">The i-dot becomes a separate orange circle — the “call coming in” pulse. The symbol puts the same dot inside the V, so wordmark and monogram share one idea.</p>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:263.5px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg></div><div class="panel dark"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:263.5px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg></div></div>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:96px;width:90.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:60.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:30.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:22.5px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:15.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sA"/></svg></div>
+<div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:48px;width:197.6px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:131.7px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:98.8px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:65.9px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg></div></div>
+<table><tr><td>Distinctiveness</td><td class='dots'>●●●○○</td></tr><tr><td>Legibility @16px</td><td class='dots'>●●●●●</td></tr><tr><td>Trademark-ability</td><td class='dots'>●●●○○</td></tr><tr><td>System fit (symbol, loader, favicon)</td><td class='dots'>●●●●●</td></tr></table><p class="verdict">Strongest at small sizes and the only one that scales cleanly into a favicon, loader and avatar. Weakness: a coloured i-dot is a common device; ownability comes from dot + V together, not the dot alone.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Concept B — Voice bars</h2><p class="idea">Both e-crossbars become orange bars — two level-meter bars sitting in the word. In the symbol, two bars of unequal height sit in the V.</p>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:264.9px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg></div><div class="panel dark"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:264.9px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg></div></div>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:96px;width:90.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:60.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:30.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:22.5px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:15.0px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sB"/></svg></div>
+<div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:48px;width:198.6px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:132.4px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:99.3px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:66.2px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wB"/></svg></div></div>
+<table><tr><td>Distinctiveness</td><td class='dots'>●●●●○</td></tr><tr><td>Legibility @16px</td><td class='dots'>●●●○○</td></tr><tr><td>Trademark-ability</td><td class='dots'>●●●●○</td></tr><tr><td>System fit (symbol, loader, favicon)</td><td class='dots'>●●●○○</td></tr></table><p class="verdict">Most ownable idea, but below ~24px the orange bars merge into a strike-through and the e’s lose their eye. The two-bar symbol is busy at 16px.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Concept C — Uptick V</h2><p class="idea">The right arm of the V rises past the cap line and its tip turns orange — recovered revenue.</p>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:237.7px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg></div><div class="panel dark"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:237.7px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg></div></div>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:96px;width:81.4px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:54.3px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:27.1px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:20.4px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:13.6px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sC"/></svg></div>
+<div class="panel light sizes"><svg class="g" style="height:48px;width:178.3px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:32px;width:118.9px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:24px;width:89.1px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg><svg class="g" style="height:16px;width:59.4px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wC"/></svg></div></div>
+<table><tr><td>Distinctiveness</td><td class='dots'>●●●○○</td></tr><tr><td>Legibility @16px</td><td class='dots'>●●●●○</td></tr><tr><td>Trademark-ability</td><td class='dots'>●●○○○</td></tr><tr><td>System fit (symbol, loader, favicon)</td><td class='dots'>●●○○○</td></tr></table><p class="verdict">Reads as a check-mark/“broken V” and the orange chip looks detached. Risk of resembling existing V-tick marks. Not recommended.</p></article>
+<article class="card"><h2>Typographic test — Title case vs lowercase</h2><p class="idea">Concept A in both cases. Title case is shipped: the capital V is the same V as the monogram, and the dot sits tight against the i stem; lowercase “v” is too small to anchor the word and the dot floats.</p>
+<div class="row"><div class="panel light"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:263.5px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wA"/></svg></div><div class="panel light"><svg class="g" style="height:64px;width:248.8px" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#wAl"/></svg></div></div></article></div>
+<section class="reco"><h2>Recommendation: Concept A</h2><p class="lead">It is the only concept that stays legible at 16 px, and its single idea (a pulse dot) transfers to the monogram, the animated loader and the favicon without redrawing anything. See the honest self-review in the delivery notes: the dot alone is not trademark-strong, so a professional should refine the V and the dot relationship before filing.</p></section>
+</main></body></html>
